dataSourcesTreatmentAndRepresentativenes.dataSelectionAndCombinationPrinciples:
Good consistency of data and LCI modeling. 
Cases where average values have been used:
- definition of the weights of the representative product, through weighted average among different products evaluated in the LCA studies present in the literature and in the available EPDs;
- primary data are re-proportioned with respect to the weights of the average product representative of the Italian supply chain; 
- the recycled content of 20% represents the average percentage of PVC-U recycled content in Italy, confirmed also by primary data collected; 
- a worst-case primary (average) transport distance was used among the primary data collected;
- distances for the transportation: 20 km for the transport of process waste to landfill, 160 km for the transport of waste to the recycling plant (according to Stichnothe and Azapagic, 2014);
- for steel production: European average production (EUROFER, 2020), consisting of 60% steel from blast furnaces and 40% from electric furnaces.
